# Task FEATURE-010-US-003-T02 — Test & verify: Executive summary, strengths, weaknesses

> **DaemonCore coding-agent prompt.** Work type: `feature` · Size: `S` · Priority: `P2` · Status: `todo`

## Where this fits
- **Epic EPIC-010 — AI Model Analysis.** Generate AI critiques that explain policy models in plain language (executive summary, strengths, weaknesses, hidden trade-offs, implementation risks, socio-economic impacts, alternatives) while keeping scoring strictly deterministic. AI interprets; it never scores.
- **Feature FEATURE-010 — AI Model Analysis — implementation.**
- **Story FEATURE-010-US-003 — Executive summary, strengths, weaknesses.** _As a user, I want a clear summary and pros/cons so I quickly grasp my model._

## Objective
Add automated tests and verify acceptance for: Executive summary, strengths, weaknesses.

## What to do
Write **deterministic automated tests** that cover each acceptance criterion of the parent story:
- Assert: All three sections generated and grounded in model data
- Assert: Output clearly labelled AI-generated
Use fixed, hand-computed numbers (see `tests/test_fiscal_model.py`). Avoid randomness, network calls and time-dependence.

## Acceptance criteria (Definition of Done)
- [ ] Automated tests cover the story's acceptance criteria
- [ ] Tests are deterministic and pass in CI
- [ ] New/updated tests pass and cover the above
- [ ] No regression in the existing `pytest` suite

## Dependencies
Complete these first: `FEATURE-010-US-003-T01`.

## Project conventions
- Target Python 3.13. Use British spelling in all user-facing text.
- Keep the pure model layer (`model/`) free of Streamlit; `app.py` is UI/render only.
- Pin any new runtime deps in `requirements.txt`; test-only deps in `requirements-dev.txt`.
- Write deterministic `pytest` tests; follow the style of `tests/test_fiscal_model.py`.
- Match the surrounding code style. Prefer small, coherent diffs over broad refactors.
- Update `README.md` / `docs/` whenever behaviour changes.

## Guardrails (EPIC-010)
- AI explains the model; it MUST NOT influence the score (scoring stays EPIC-003).
- Ground all critique in the model's actual inputs, outputs and scores.
- Label output clearly as AI-generated; route calls via the EPIC-008 framework.

## Verification
- `python3 -m py_compile <changed .py files>`
- `python3 -m pytest -q` — all tests pass (add/extend tests for this change).

## Notes
- This simulator is a transparent scenario sandbox, not an official forecast — keep that framing in any user-facing text.
- If requirements are ambiguous or you must change a public interface, stop and flag it rather than guessing.
